    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d958">

                <pb facs="0852" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3016.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 4, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Brigadier General Duncan, commanding
                    Department Texas, telegraphs from Fort Sam Houston, Tex., March 4, the
                    following: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>From Colonel Steever:</p>
                        <p>“Fighting in Chihuahua began this morning. Villa, loyal to Madero,
                            attacked Orozco, who quit Madero 1st instant. Salazar, appealed to by
                            Orozco, is entraining men to go south to Orozco’s assistance. Probably
                            over 4,000 rebels in Juarez, largely mounted. Additions daily. More
                            disorder in Juarez not improbable.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. L. Stimson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
